{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Like streams they stretch.</b> For indeed the synagogues and houses of study for the multitudes of Israel are like streams that stretch toward the fields to water them; and likewise the dwellers in tents — the masters of Torah — draw and give drink from their Torah to the multitudes. And similarly, those who pray are like gardens beside a river, which never cease bearing fruit, as they said, of blessed memory (Rosh HaShanah 17): ״A covenant sealed for the thirteen attributes, which never return empty.״"], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:40:59.172389267Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}